      "writtenOn": "2022-02-07T22:20:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "exception_panic \u003d Interrupt vector table\ntask_clear_pending_irq \u003d clock-f.c in reset_rtc_alarm\nmutex_lock, mutex_unlock, in_interrupt_context \u003d bkpdata.c in bkpdata_write\n\nsystem_set_reset_flags \u003c- Should be removed now that system_pre_init()\u0027s call is gone.\n\nInterrupts are disabled with no threading during the Boot Manager so task_clear_pending_irq, in_interrupt_context, mutex_lock, mutex_unlock are either constant returns or non-ops.\n\nexception_panic() likely needs to be replaced. The standard panic handlers store variables, print a message, and then issue a reboot but that\u0027s not likely going to be useful in this case. The most likely cause of a fault during this limited operation is the reset vector that the application jumps to and/or it\u0027s vector table are invalid. A system reset won\u0027t allow a recovery by itself unless the CONFIG_DFU_BOOTMANAGER_MAX_REBOOT_COUNT flag is set as well. We likely want it to reset into DFU.",
      "parentUuid": "40ec6641_2d6244b0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 214,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 214,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "058837d0becbec73f2bd50c7dbcbbc9ac32c95f6",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
